1.) docker compose -p chapter6 -f ".\docker\docker-compose.chapter6.yml" ps

2.) Invoke-RestMethod `
    -Uri "http://localhost:8073/eureka/apps/organization-service" `
    -Headers @{ Accept = "application/json" } |
    ConvertTo-Json -Depth 10

3.) 1.) Invoke-RestMethod `
        -Uri "http://localhost:8082/v1/organization/d898a142-de44-466c-8c88-9ceb2c2429d3/license/f2a9c9d4-d2c0-44fa-97fe-724d77173c62/discovery" `
        -Method Get | Format-List

    2.) Invoke-RestMethod `
        -Uri "http://localhost:8082/v1/organization/d898a142-de44-466c-8c88-9ceb2c2429d3/license/f2a9c9d4-d2c0-44fa-97fe-724d77173c62/rest" `
        -Method Get | Format-List

    3.) Invoke-RestMethod `
        -Uri "http://localhost:8082/v1/organization/d898a142-de44-466c-8c88-9ceb2c2429d3/license/f2a9c9d4-d2c0-44fa-97fe-724d77173c62/feign" `
        -Method Get | Format-List
        
4.) licensing-service
        └── src
            └── main
                └── java
                    └── com.optimagrowth.license.service.client
                        ├── OrganizationDiscoveryClient.java
                        ├── OrganizationRestTemplateClient.java
                        └── OrganizationFeignClient.java

    "This concludes my Chapter 6 demonstration.
    I have successfully configured the Config Server, 
    Eureka Server, Licensing Service and Organization Service.
    I have also demonstrated that both microservices register 
    with Eureka and that the Licensing Service can communicate 
    with the Organization Service using DiscoveryClient, RestTemplate and Feign.
    All three approaches returned the expected results."